From 04659de069381123029cfc267ab4221bcb559390 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cute-johnny <269855522+cute-johnny@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:05:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Support dictionaries larger than 16 MiB (format v203)

Binary v202 dictionaries store children and bigram pointers in at most
3 bytes, so files over 16 MiB get truncated pointers. The keyboard then
reads garbage (corrupt suggestions) and crashes during swipe typing.

Add format version 203: same layout as v202, but the "three bytes"
address type is stored in 4 bytes. The v2 reader gets a largeAddresses
flag that is enabled for v203 files. Stock readers reject v203 as
unknown instead of misreading it.

Also add a patched AOSP encoder (tools/large-dict) that writes v203 and
refuses to write corrupt v202 files over 16 MiB, plus a GitHub Actions
workflow that builds the unstable APK. README notes this is a modified fork.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
